summary: Duplicates: list the groups of byte-identical files, or scan for them

!! Reference

```
Duplicates: list the groups of byte-identical files, or scan for them

The scan writes its conclusion — one `duplicate_group` metarecord per set, referenced by its members through `mfr_duplicate_group` — so the listing is an ordinary query and "what else is identical to this file" is `same(mfr_duplicate_group, <uuid>)`. Nothing here deletes a file.

Usage: mf duplicate [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list   List the duplicate groups, worst reclaimable space first — the default
  scan   Scan for byte-identical files and record the groups
  clear  Delete every duplicate group and every link to one (the hashes are kept)
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
